   "design": "An ID scanner at the cage reads the document's machine-readable zone and photo page into the account form, and stores the image with the account. This replaces typing details and photocopying, and the worker checks the fields. On saving, the account system queries the exclusion register and sanctions list with those details, instead of the worker retyping them into portals; the worker handles any hit. The system lists new accounts per shift, so the spreadsheet ends. Talking with the patron, inspecting the ID, setting limits, signing and checking stay with the worker.",
   "approvals": [],
   "previous_blocker": "ID details were typed three times: into the account system and two portals.",
   "enabler_now": "ID scanners and register checks linked to the account system.",
   "still_hard": "Foreign IDs without a readable zone.",
   "human_edge": "Seeing that the patron does not match the photo.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less typing; identity checks stay.",
